{
 "method": "Five registered photographs independently sampled at the recessed sash plane. In the upper unobstructed part of each ground and second-floor window, 27 scanlines cross each jamb. The difference in intensity between bands centred 48 mm either side of each candidate identifies a light-to-dark or dark-to-light edge. At least two photographs with median contrast >=22 and >=17 positive strips must agree within 0.10 m. Wires, hedges and trees can leave edges unresolved. Raw values and image endpoints are retained.",
